<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Willem Kieft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1597–1647</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Willem Kieft was Director of New Netherland from 1638 to 1647. His attempt to tax the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a> and other local peoples, and the massacres at Pavonia and Corlears Hook in 1643, provoked Kieft's War of 1643 to 1645, which devastated the colony. Recalled after settlers complained, he died in 1647 when the ship carrying him back to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> was wrecked.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/willem-kieft.jpg" alt="Willem Kieft" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reproduction of painting by Charles Bescler Co. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Willem_(Wilhelm)_Kieft_(1597-1647)_Director_of_New_Netherland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
